1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,040
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!

2
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,578
You're on the move!

3
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,035
You're teetering on the edge
of the Shadow Realm, Yugi.

4
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:12,080
One false move and you'll
be trapped for eternity.

5
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:18,057
Yeah, well if I were you, I
wouldn't get my hopes up, Akura.

6
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:19,180
And why not?

7
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:22,820
Thanks to the special effect
of my cursed twin dolls,

8
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:28,017
every card that was sent to my former
graveyard was just released onto the field.

9
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,100
But you, on the other hand...

10
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:33,460
Well, let's just say
you've seen better duels.

11
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,999
Too bad you can't bring out
the Pharaoh to save you.

12
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,440
Maybe not, but I can save him!

13
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:42,914
Just as soon as I beat Bakura
and get out of this place!

14
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:48,060
Now that my twins are
finished, why don't you go? Ha!

15
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:49,960
I was hoping you'd say that!

16
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,680
Not so fast!

17
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:56,377
I'm afraid you just triggered the
special effect of my necro-soldier.

18
00:01:56,460 --> 00:02:00,780
As long as he remains on the
field, every time your turn begins,

19
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,480
my necro army increases by one.

20
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,820
And since this ability applies
to my new soldier as well,

21
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,747
I now have an army of three.

22
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,560
As you were.

23
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:17,569
How's Yugi supposed to beat an
army of little zombie freaks?

24
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:22,886
Actually, since each of his soldiers has
zero points, it shouldn't be too tough.

25
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,700
Here goes!

26
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:29,040
First, my Silent Swordsman jumps
to level 5 with 3500 points!

27
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,085
But that's just the beginning!

28
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:35,044
To accompany my Silent Swordsman,
I'll summon my Silent Magician!

29
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,140
Now, Marshmellon,

30
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:45,100
Silent Swordsman and Silent Magician
attack all three of his Necro-soldiers!

31
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,410
Alright!

32
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,860
Once Vakura's troop of
Necro-corps is gone, Yugi wins!

33
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,760
No way!

34
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,777
But why did my swordsman stop?

35
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,389
It doesn't make any sense!

36
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,877
Of course it does.

37
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,260
I've played my narrow corridor track.

38
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,887
Yeah, and what does that do?

39
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,060
I'm glad you asked, Wheeler.

40
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,797
This handy track card
prevents your friends from

41
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:21,617
attacking with more than two
monsters in any given turn.

42
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:24,960
And might I remind you,
my graveyard's gone,

43
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:29,395
so the soldiers you just destroyed
shall return to the field as spirits.

44
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:36,040
I hope you don't mind if my phantom
monsters stick around to watch me win.

45
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:41,377
What I want to know is, what's he
planning to do with all those monsters?

46
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:43,180
I'll take over from here.

47
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,784
Oh, did I mention my
magician's special ability?

48
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:50,840
When you draw, he jumps up one
level and gains 500 points!

49
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,360
Should I be impressed?

50
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,420
Ah, just the card I was hoping to see.

51
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:03,240
The time has come to
reveal my true strategy.

52
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,320
True strategy?

53
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,140
Yes, is that an echo in here?

54
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,440
Behold my counterbalance magic card.

55
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,720
What does that do?

56
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:17,040
As long as this card remains on the field,

57
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,437
each of us must transfer a
certain number of cards from

58
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:25,017
our deck to our graveyard at
the end of our turn how many

59
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:29,657
you ask you must discard as
many cards as there are monsters

60
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:34,760
on the field of course that
includes my phantom monsters

61
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:40,537
no way then we'd be throwing
out practically our entire deck

62
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:44,120
but why would you play a card
that puts you at risk also.

63
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:45,969
It doesn't make any sense.

64
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:50,380
To work, it requires a graveyard.

65
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,520
And I don't have one.

66
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,016
Guess that means I can't participate.

67
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,920
I feel so left out.

68
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,740
So you're in this alone.

69
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,150
Get it?

70
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:03,000
This card only drains your deck.

71
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:05,980
So that was your plan all along.

72
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,926
You wanted to force me
to get rid of my cards.

73
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,780
Oh, man.

74
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,760
Yuki's only got a few turns left. What?

75
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,240
And it only gets worse.

76
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,145
For now, I summon another
monster to the field.

77
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,680
Necro Mannequin!

78
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,680
But that's not all.

79
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,940
Next, I activate the trap card.

80
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,400
Necro Cycle!

81
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:32,480
As long as my mannequin
remains on the field,

82
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:36,582
this trap allows me to automatically
summon another one each turn.

83
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,360
Look at all those monsters!

84
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:45,580
And just think, every one of them
represents a card you're going to lose!

85
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:53,340
And all the fun begins in your next move,

86
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,940
so I see no need to drag
the suspense out any longer!

87
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,940
I end my turn!

88
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:11,400
Stand back, I shall handle this

89
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,440
No, Sork is mine My king,

90
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:18,877
please don't It's the only way
We've tried everything in our power

91
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:25,060
But nothing works There's one hope
left And it lies in my hand Sork,

92
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,057
you've invaded my kingdom
And threatened my people

93
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:32,040
And now you must pay for
your crime Millennium puzzle,

94
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:33,180
activate

95
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:44,360
And now I shall call upon
the three Egyptian gods!

96
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:49,940
Obelus the Tormentor, Slifer the Sky
Dragon, and the Winged Dragon of Ra!

97
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,700
Your fate is now sealed!

98
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:20,860
Behold, the gods of Egypt!

99
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,800
Well, it appears the game
has shifted in my favor.

100
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,440
Your creatures are no match for Zok.

101
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,641
I should know since he and
I are one and the same!

102
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,030
Hold on.

103
00:07:34,113 --> 00:07:36,760
You mean, you are Zork?

104
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,350
Surprise?

105
00:07:40,433 --> 00:07:41,920
How's that for a twist?

106
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:45,540
Now, let's go in for a
closer look, shall we?

107
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,940
Surrender now, Zork!

108
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:03,900
Or face the rage of the
three Egyptian gods!

109
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:14,420
When I am through with them, your deities
shall bow before the Lord of Darkness!

110
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,177
No way! It's them!

111
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:23,340
Slifer, Obelisk, and Ra!

112
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:26,720
But they seem way too
realistic to be holograms.

113
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,469
Can they be the real deal?

114
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:30,530
Obelisk!

115
00:08:30,613 --> 00:08:32,009
The first attack is yours!

116
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,660
Strike him down with your fist of fate!

117
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,960
Nice shot!

118
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:52,020
Not a bad start, but let's
see if Yugi can keep this up.

119
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,660
Light for the Sky Dragon!

120
00:08:57,940 --> 00:09:00,764
Lay down your judgment
upon this enemy of Egypt!

121
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:10,520
Finally, Winged Dragon of Roar!

122
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,189
May your eternal light
banish the darkness!

123
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:30,720
Now, my friends, combine
your strength and end this!

124
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:36,620
Fist of Fury, Thunder Force
Attack, and Blaze Cannon Blast!

125
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,180
Finish him off!

126
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:15,680
It's over.

127
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:16,820
We're saved.

128
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,680
Let's hope so.

129
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,340
Look, the darkness has lifted.

130
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,720
Finally, Zork is gone.

131
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:37,600
All hail the Egyptian gods. We're free.

132
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:40,380
You did it, Pharaoh. We did.

133
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,010
Zork.

134
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,300
Get back.

135
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,520
Can it be?

136
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:54,940
Don't do it! Our sun!

137
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,220
What's he doing?

138
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:01,620
He's covering Egypt in complete darkness!

139
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:09,460
Somehow that thing just
caused a solar eclipse.

140
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,980
Egyptian gods, attack
before the light is gone!

141
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:14,100
Please, hurry!

142
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:28,120
As the darkness spreads,
my strength grows!

143
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,477
Die!

144
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:32,960
It's almost gone!

145
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:39,280
Raw and sliver, attack!

146
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:51,020
Without the sun's rays, you
are powerless against me!

147
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,880
Now prepare to be
consumed by the darkness!

148
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:17,760
The Egyptian gods! He beat them! But how?

149
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:19,137
This can't be!

150
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:20,573
That was our last hope.

151
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,580
We lost. That's nuts.

152
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:24,825
No one defeats those monsters.

153
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:30,540
There is nothing left to do.

154
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,320
Now all hope is lost.

155
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:38,380
Your Egyptian gods are shadows
of their former selves.

156
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:41,980
Let them crumble along with your hope.

157
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:48,380
Carol, no!

158
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,950
Remember,

159
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:57,560
you lose a card for every monster on the
field, and so far there are ten Oh yeah?

160
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:04,680
Not for long First, my silent swordsman
increases one level and 500 points Hold on,

161
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,560
your monsters aren't the only ones
who can do tricks Necro-mannequin,

162
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,560
show Yugi your newest talent

163
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:16,420
Now there's a total of
11 monsters on the field

164
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:20,177
How's Yugi supposed to get
rid of all those monsters?

165
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:24,757
I mean, didn't Bakura play some card
that limits Yugi's attacks or something?

166
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:25,740
Right you are.

167
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,720
Narrow Corridor, to be exact.

168
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:31,300
And it limits Yugi to two
attacks per turn. Plus,

169
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,080
thanks to my Necro Twins,

170
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:37,181
whatever monsters he destroys will
return to the field as phantoms.

171
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:38,580
We'll see.

172
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:43,517
First, my swordsman will attack your
Necro Soldier with Silent Sword Slash.

173
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:48,860
And then I'm sending my Silent Magician
to destroy your Necro Mannequin! Now go!

174
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:55,797
Not bad, but your turn is over.

175
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,900
And you know what that means.

176
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,420
Eleven cards go to your graveyard.

177
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:05,860
Now, if my math is correct, that
leaves seventeen cards in your deck.

178
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,960
And once they're all gone, game over.

179
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:10,610
However,

180
00:14:10,693 --> 00:14:12,937
my twins will make sure
your turn doesn't end on

181
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:16,440
a sour note by giving you
1,200 extra life points.

182
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:17,760
Sounds good to me.

183
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,180
And why are you so chipper?

184
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:23,077
Well, for one, my magician
just got stronger.

185
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:26,395
It's going to take much more
than that to save you now.

186
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,240
I just summoned my Necro Wall.

187
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,697
This lets me increase my
monster army by adding Necro

188
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,877
Wall tokens equal to the
number of zombies on the field,

189
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:39,140
Which gives me two extra monsters.

190
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,140
He cared. He did.

191
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:46,477
Now say hello to the two newest additions
to my ever-growing collection of monsters.

192
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,757
Necro Wall Token No.

193
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,380
1 and Necro Wall Token No. 2.

194
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,840
That gives me a grand total of 14.

195
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:54,891
Now make your final move.

196
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,400
This duel's not over yet, Makura.

197
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,760
First, my Swordsman gets a boost.

198
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,317
Now get ready for another double attack.

199
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,857
Silent Swordsman attack
is wall token number

200
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:07,764
one and Silent Magician
attack token number two!

201
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:15,200
Very impressive, Yugi.

202
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:20,369
Unfortunately, since you've used up your
two attack limit, your turn is over.

203
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:25,800
That may be true, but I can still
activate my aria from beyond magic card!

204
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:28,397
It allows me to choose
any magic card that has

205
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:31,680
already been removed from
the game and reactivate it!

206
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:34,277
And I choose one of yours!

207
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,980
Spirit Sword of Sailing!

208
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:40,840
And I'm using it to imprison
one of my own monsters!

209
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:42,820
My Silent Swordsman!

210
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:50,840
Is it me, or did he just
harpoon his best card?

211
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,020
That's so weird!

212
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:55,797
Bacora has a field full of
monsters, and Yuki targets his own?

213
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:57,357
That ends my turn!

214
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,100
Glad to hear it.

215
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:01,920
Now then, discard 11 cards.

216
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:07,840
You may gain a few life points,
but you lose most of your deck.

217
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:16,440
Just one more turn, and all
of your cards will be gone.

218
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:20,040
And victory will be mine.

219
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:27,080
You know, I probably could
end my turn right now.

220
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:30,397
forcing you to discard the
rest of your deck immediately.

221
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:33,715
But I think watching you
squirm would be much more fun.

222
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,620
So instead, I'll summon my
Necro-Jar in attack mode.

223
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,700
Now attack his silent magician!

224
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,360
But why?

225
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:46,721
Yeah, doesn't Yuki's monster have
more attack points than Vakora's?

226
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,300
You just gave up almost
all of your life points!

227
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,080
Why would you do that?

228
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:56,700
Good question.

229
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,620
It was all a part of my master plan.

230
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,220
You see, thanks to my Necrochar,

231
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:06,297
you must discard one card for
every 300 points I just lost.

232
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:12,240
And since my damage was 1,400, you
lose four cards from your deck.

233
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:15,640
So off to the graveyard they go.

234
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,220
Wait a second.

235
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:20,480
That's gonna leave Yugi
with only one card left.

236
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:26,077
And so the end is here.

237
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:30,500
Not only the end of our duel, but
the end of the world as we know it.

238
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:34,977
Why, with you trapped in the Shadow
Realm, the pharaoh will never defeat Sork.

239
00:17:35,060 --> 00:17:36,820
Now let's review, shall we?

240
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:43,280
Twelve monsters remain on the field, and
you have only one card left in your deck.

241
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:47,380
And as we all know, when you
run out of cards, you lose.

242
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,160
I knew it all along.

243
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:52,840
Without the pharaoh, you're nothing.

244
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,240
He's the king of games.

245
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,384
You're just a frightened child.

246
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:02,060
Yugi, don't listen to
a word this creep says.

247
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:03,221
You can do this.

248
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:04,619
Tay is right, pal.

249
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:06,617
He's just trying to psych you out.

250
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,530
That's all.

251
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:10,460
I'm the only one being honest with you.

252
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:13,919
Think about every important
duel you've ever fought.

253
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,740
Who was doing all the work?

254
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,560
The Pharaoh, that's who.

255
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,760
Maybe he's right.

256
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:33,480
Yuki, I can't do this without you.

257
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:35,500
Please, help me.

258
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:39,040
The future of mankind depends on it.

259
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,760
The barrow needs me.

260
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:45,200
And this duel's still on.

261
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:48,020
I have one cart left
and that's all I need.

262
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,620
That's the spirit.

263
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:50,940
Now win.

264
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:54,140
What do you expect to do with one card?

265
00:18:55,980 --> 00:19:01,320
I sacrificed my marshmallow and my
silent magician so I can summon this!

266
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,878
Gandorra, the Dragon of Destruction!

267
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,330
Not that!

268
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:11,450
Makura,

269
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:14,577
the game's not over till
the last card is played and

270
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:18,880
my last card is the one with
the power to stop you! But how?

271
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,857
I have a field full of monsters!

272
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,280
and you only have one!

273
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:30,460
Gandora, activate your special ability!

274
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:33,660
Boundless Giga Rays!

275
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:38,880
No!
